# Regression (host output vs host goldens) tolerance, read by harness/check.sh.
# First non-comment line: <fb mismatch fraction> [<.state numeric tolerance>]
# The host goldens were generated on a different libc/libm than the CI runner (ubuntu-24.04), so
# a few pixels along rasterised edges or a last-digit state difference are expected. 0.0005 of
# 96000 px is 48 px; 0.001 is the state tolerance (states print 3-4 decimals). Identical files
# always pass without consulting these. Set the first value to 0 to demand exact frames.
0.0005 0.001
